# No trailing slash: `.venv/` matches a directory only, and a git worktree's
# natural way to get one is a *symlink* to the main checkout's. That left the
# symlink untracked and one `git add -A` from being committed — and worse, a
# worktree without it silently skips `CLIRunnerTests`'s real-`rich` test, which
# reports as a green run with one skip rather than as a gap in verification.
.venv
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.superpowers/
.DS_Store
build/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/
.worktrees/

# Large binary artifacts that occasionally end up in the working tree
*.ipa
*.deb
*.profraw

# Xcode DerivedData, pinned to the repo by scripts/graft-install.
#
# The glob rather than the exact name: concurrent agents need *separate*
# derived-data paths, because two `xcodebuild` runs sharing one path collide.
# The first time that happened the second path — `.derived-data-b/` — was not
# covered here and reached 561MB of untracked content, a single `git add -A`
# from being committed.
.derived-data*/

# bagbak 4.x scratch dir. `decrypt_runner` now runs it with `cwd` set to the
# temp dump directory so our own dumps no longer land one here — this is for
# bagbak invoked by hand from the repo root, which still does.
.bagbak/

# Decrypted apps, signing material, injected libraries and secrets never
# belong in the repo.
decrypted/
*.dylib
*.p12
*.p8
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
.env

# Local tool state.
.claude/
.ruff_cache/
